    "bottomLine": "A contractor-grade way to stiffen loose joint sand and enhance color in one pass, if you can get the joints fully dry first.",
    "description": "SEK Surebond has been selling paver sealers to installers for decades, and SB-6000 is its water-based product for interlocking pavers. The headline feature is the joints. When it is flooded into dry joint sand, it soaks down and binds the top layer of grains, which slows washout from storms and hose-downs and makes it harder for weeds and ants to settle in. On the paver faces it gives a moderate color enhancement with a low sheen. It is a practical choice for patios that already have ordinary sand joints where digging out and re-sanding with polymeric sand would be a big job. The weak point is the same as every joint-stabilizing sealer: it only works on a full, dry joint. Refill the sand first, sweep it clean off the faces, wait for a dry stretch, and expect to use noticeably more product than the paver faces alone would need."
